# Agent Observability Dashboard

Self-hosted observability for AI agents: ingest spans (LLM calls, tool calls), browse traces, and track token usage, cost, latency, and errors — all in one place, nothing leaves your machine.

## Quickstart

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
uvicorn agent_obs.app:app --reload
```

Open http://localhost:8000 for the dashboard.

### Docker

```bash
docker build -t agent-obs .
docker run -p 8000:8000 agent-obs
```

## Instrumenting an agent

POST one JSON span per LLM call or tool invocation:

```bash
curl -X POST localhost:8000/api/events -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{
  "trace_id": "run-42",
  "span_id": "llm-1",
  "kind": "llm",
  "name": "planner",
  "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
  "input_tokens": 1200,
  "output_tokens": 300,
  "latency_ms": 840,
  "status": "ok"
}'
```

Span fields: `trace_id`, `span_id`, `parent_span_id` (optional), `kind` (`llm`|`tool`), `name`, `model`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `latency_ms`, `status` (`ok`|`error`), `meta` (free-form dict).

## API

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/events` | Ingest a span (201) |
| GET | `/api/traces` | List traces with span/token/latency/error rollups |
| GET | `/api/traces/{id}` | Spans in one trace |
| GET | `/api/stats` | Totals: spans, tokens, error rate, p50/p95 latency, est. cost, per-model usage |
| GET | `/` | Dashboard UI |

## Tests

```bash
pytest -q
```

CI runs the suite on every push.

## Notes

- Storage is SQLite (`:memory:` by default); point `Store(path=...)` at a file for persistence.
- Prices in `src/agent_obs/prices.py` are sample figures — verify against provider pricing before relying on cost estimates.

## Roadmap

- Persistent file-backed store + retention policy
- Trace waterfall view in the UI
- Alerting on error-rate / cost thresholds
- OpenTelemetry span ingestion
